        "id": 1944425
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T14:04:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @tweek@google.com, if my understanding correct, here we want to use the flag as build-time flag. If so, only adding `is_fixed_read_only` is enough. The mode `force-read-only` is for flags are not `fixed_read_only`, but the library is desired to be used as a share, read-only library.",
      "parentUuid": "4687b53a_271cff70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6a1d5b6_4b5e11b9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T23:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @zhidou@google.com, thanks for that. That is correct, we want a build-time only flag. I just ran the test locally by removing `force-read-only` from Android.bp. This raises the error `dependency \"server_configurable_flags\" of \"libselinux_aconfig_flags_c_lib\" missing variant`. (We definitely don\u0027t want to add this dependency). IIUC, it looks like this is a bug in Soong?",
      "parentUuid": "0d5d7b57_1cfa4817",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0629fb69_b54c6b76",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882770
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T16:08:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the reason server_configruable_flags is missing some variant is because in libselinux, we have:\n\n    ramdisk_available: true,\n    vendor_ramdisk_available: true,\n    \nBut this is not present for server_configurable_flags, if we add the following two lines to server_configurable_flags, the build should work.",
      "parentUuid": "b6a1d5b6_4b5e11b9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3cd5076_054cf93d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882770
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T16:11:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For context, we have been adding variants of server_configurable_flags over the time (each time we run into a missing variant error like this one). We should update server_configurable_flags.",
      "parentUuid": "0629fb69_b54c6b76",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "734edd26_7fa4ef5d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T23:42:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. I\u0027m a bit puzzled by this answer. The intent here is to have a build-time only flag. From the documentation: \"The flag is a build-time flag, and its value is embedded in the code.\" I don\u0027t understand why we would need to rely on this library if we are not using any of its functionality.\n\nlibselinux is used early in the boot code (part of the 2nd stage init), I am not even sure that this library functions are available/useful that early. (see also b/326303058).\n\nIt\u0027s not because we can make that library available that we should if this makes little sense architecturally.",
      "parentUuid": "c3cd5076_054cf93d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd7b45f4_c58b86a9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882770
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T14:35:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason why server_configurable_flags are added as dependency is because build system has no way to tell if all flags in an aconfig package are all read only. We allow a mix of force read only and regular read write flag in one aconfig package. So when this aconfig package needs codegen, we have to assume the worst and add this dependency.\n\nOn the other hand, when using force read only mode codegen. All flags in the package is converted to read only during codegen, so we can safely remove that dependency. That is why it works when you use force read only codegen.\n\nCurrently, persistent system property (which server_configurable_flags is querying) is available after /data partition mount, so after 2nd stage init. But for new storage, we are moving the actual flag storage into /metadata partition which will be available much early on.",
      "parentUuid": "734edd26_7fa4ef5d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cc6b858_5f4635e2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944425
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T16:44:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Thiébaud, I have discussed with Dennis. If you don\u0027t want to make the change on server_configurable_flags, you can use the force-read-only mode for now. \n\nPlease note, the force-read-only mode is not designed for this purpose, and it is mutually exclusive with the exportable flags. Which means if in the same declaration, there are exportable flags, and non-exportable flags, the force-read-only mode library will only include the non-exportable flags.\n\nPlease add a TODO comment and tag this bug b/326414126. We will clean this up once the new storage is in place.",
      "parentUuid": "cd7b45f4_c58b86a9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29a6be6b_81001f66",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
