      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T05:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@enh@google.com From my understanding, toybox now includes libselinux as a shared library (toybox-shared-defaults), so this may not be an issue anymore. Thoughts?",
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a71cd9b7_7114152f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T15:58:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, there are other ways that libc++ ends up in running toybox processes too:\n```\n    // This doesn\u0027t actually prevent us from dragging in libc++ at runtime\n    // on the device because libnetd_client.so is C++, but it improves host\n    // startup time.\n    stl: \"none\",\n```\n(and since the _host_ toybox doesn\u0027t use libselinux, this doesn\u0027t make host startup times worse.)",
      "parentUuid": "29a6be6b_81001f66",
      "revId": "b76d6ccda33c37cb0ae0c778cc43b5146e1571c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
